:: OC Jonny The Fret Champion [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
You step into the arcade and are once again greeted with the exciting sounds of various machines going off around you against the backdrop of classical 90s music, combined with children’s laughter and frustration. You’ve been here before, but you always seem to find new games you haven’t seen or played before. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Brimming with excitement to try something new, you start looking around the arcade to satisfy your craving.</span> <br>
<br>
After 10 minutes of walking around trying to find some more unique games to play, the sounds of clicking and clacking echo from the back end of the arcade. You’ve never explored this part of the arcade, since most of the machines are much older games that only a few kids and older adults tend to enjoy, but these repetitive clicking sounds stir your curiosity. <br>
<br>
You make your way around a set of old pinball machines when suddenly a lone boy comes into your view, holding a plastic guitar that’s attached to a slightly dusty machine that reads <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Fret Champion.”</span> <br>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Mouth: "Happy",
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "OC Jonny",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Everyday",
            Eyes: "Tired",
            Mouth: "Smirk",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

Despite being taller than you, the boy looks roughly the same age as you due to his boyish appearance. He’s really skinny and sports an older rock-and-roll look with a sleeveless jean jacket over a black tank top, ripped skinny black jeans, aviators, and a top hat, with long, flowing dark brown hair straggling down past his neck. <span style="Color: Pink">You even notice the sag of his jeans, which shows off a peak of his black boxers around his big butt that accents well in his skinny jeans.</span> Something about the way he dresses seems familiar, but you can’t put your finger on it. <br>
<br>

<<if $Player.Traits.includes("Virtuso")>>
    <span style="Color: LightGreen">You have a sudden realization that you have seen this look before from an old rock band your dad used to like called Swords N’ Tulips. He dresses exactly like the lead guitarist of the band, Flash. You chuckle a little bit in surprise that a boy as young as you enjoys music like that still, to the point of dressing like the main guitar player.</span> <br>
    <br>
<</if>>

The boy doesn’t notice your approach; his attention is solely focused on the game that he’s playing. The guitar he’s holding has 5 different-colored buttons that correspond on-screen to a series of gems that scroll down the fretboard for the player to hit in time with the song. The boy is really good at this game, never missing a note on what seems to be a really difficult song with a bunch of triple notes and sweeping solos. You find yourself becoming mesmerized by the game, wondering how hard it would be to play. <br>
<br>
The song comes to an end, and the boy gives off a confident smirk as he crushes the previous high score of the song. <span style="Color: LightCoral">At this point, you were standing so close to him that when he turned around, he smacked you right in the head with the top of his plastic guitar.</span> The boy shrieks and jumps a little, not expecting someone to be behind him, but his face quickly turns to concern as he fixes his hat. <br>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Mouth: "Frown",
            Eyes: "Sad",
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "OC Jonny",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Everyday",
            Mouth: "Frown",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yo, I’m so sorry dude, you ok?”</span> <span style="Color: LightCoral">You rub your head where the plastic guitar hit, and even though it hurt quite a bit from the sudden impact,</span> it wasn’t enough to leave a knot thankfully. You tell him you’re ok, and he lets out a sigh of relief. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Didn’t expect anyone to be back here. You should really try to make yourself known instead of sneaking up on people.”</span> He says playfully while you try to explain yourself. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Name’s <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jonny Roswell</span>, I think I remember seeing you around school. You’re the new kid, right?”</span> You confirm this to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jonny</span>, to which he smirks again, saying <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“that’s not normal for them to accept newbies, but hey, we can always use cute new faces around Preston.”</span> <span style="Color: Pink">Did he just call you cute? <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jonny</span> snickers as you feel your face start to flush as red as the spot on your forehead.</span> <br>

<<set _ad to [
    {
        Name: "Player",
        State: {
            Blush: 1,
        },
    },
    {
        Name: "OC Jonny",
        State: {
            Outfit: "Everyday",
            Eyes: "Tired",
            Mouth: "Smirk",
        },
    },
]>>
<<ad _ad>>

He notices you staring at the game he's playing, and he smirks, giving you a half-smile. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You wanna play?”</span> He asks, picking up the other guitar and handing it to you. You give <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jonny</span> a confused look and tell him you've never played this game before. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ah, don’t worry dude, it’s not too hard!”</span> <span style="Color: Pink">As you start to mumble an excuse, he forcefully puts the guitar strap around your body, which makes you jump a little as he takes his time adjusting it to your figure.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“All you gotta do is hold down the button on the fret that matches the gem color on the screen, and when the gem passes the bar at the bottom, you hit the strum button down here!”</span> He also reassures you that there’s an <span style="Color: LightGreen">easy mode</span>, so you only need to worry about the first three colors, which seemed easy enough. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jonny</span> puts in a few quarters in the machine and picks one of the first songs on the set list titled <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Slow Drive,”</span> and you immediately hone your focus into the game. <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    <span style="Color: LightCoral">It was rough at first, hearing the disappointing sounds of missing the notes and your crowd meter dropping, which made the in-game audience boo you. You can’t help but feel embarrassed compared to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jonny</span>’s effortless playing.</span> He turns to you and gives you a smile and a slight nod, which helps instill determination in you. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Suddenly, it all clicks, and you begin to hit the notes in sync, <span style="Color: LightCoral">missing a few every now and then,</span> but you feel your confidence growing along with the crowd meter, and you’re actually having fun!</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Eyes: "Tired",
                Mouth: "Smirk",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "OC Jonny",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Eyes: "Tired",
                Mouth: "Smirk",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

    When the song ends, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jonny</span> <span style="Color: LightGreen">gives you a high five and exclaims how much better you are than most people he’s forced to play this game for the first time. He inserts more of his money into the machine, and the two of you play several more songs together, even drawing a small crowd cheering you on.</span> After the last song, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jonny</span> takes off his guitar and places it back onto the machine. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You cool man, thanks for hanging with me. Always awesome to find others who love Fret Champion. Maybe I’ll see ya around here again?”</span> You smile and nod at the boy which prompts another smirking, half-smile from <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jonny</span>. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“If you see me around school feel free to hang with us, some of us guys are looking to start a band. If you got the skill, maybe we’ll let ya try out!”</span> <span style="Color: Yellow">Your eyes grow wide from the offer, thinking how cool it would be to be in a band.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jonny</span> laughs at your expression as he reaches into his pocket to pull out a white, Kender guitar pick and hands it to you. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Something to remember me by,”</span> <span style="Color: Pink">he leans his face down enough for his stunning blue eyes to peer over his aviators and winks at you, which makes you blush a little bit.</span> <span style="Color: Yellow">He tells you that he’s usually hanging out with some of his friends in the music room after school, jamming out, and if you’re serious about joining, you should drop by so you can try out.</span> <br>
    <br>
    He grabs his skateboard that’s sitting beside the machine and bids you farewell as he starts making his way out of the arcade. What a cool kid, Opal City sure has its characters. <br>

    <<if $Player.Traits.includes("Virtuso")>>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightGreen">You think more about his offer to start a band, and you get a little nervous about the idea, wondering if you’d be skilled enough to be accepted. The nervousness gives way to thoughts of going after school to practice in someone’s garage, and then to the thought of headlining Brochella with a bunch of screaming fans rocking out to your playing. You smile and grip the guitar pick in your hand with confidence and determination, willing to at least give it a try.</span> <br>
    <</if>>

